  "notes": "Captured 2026-10-13 with WebFetch. The xbox.com homepage body is client-rendered: WebFetch saw a hero carousel whose slide copy is image-only (alt \"Lilith from Diablo IV rises behind an XBOX Series X console.\"), the \"Shop for more xbox products or sign in to your xbox account\" strip (items unpopulated in the capture) and \"Follow XBOX\"; the clone hero slide copy (GTA VI pre-order) is the clone's choice, not copied. /en-US/games/all-games/console and /en-US/search/results rendered no body (JS app); their expect strings come from research/xbox-store.md (search observed in a browser 2026-09-29). support.xbox.com is a JS shell with no content, so support topic pages summarise the known Xbox Support categories. account.microsoft.com redirects to sign-in. web.archive.org is blocked for WebFetch. microsoft.com/en-us/store/b/shipping failed; the support.microsoft.com shipping article was used instead. Off-site header/footer destinations (news.xbox.com, support.xbox.com, microsoft.com, developer.microsoft.com, gear.xbox.com, Xbox Design Lab, aka.ms feedback, the All Microsoft flyout) are local summary pages. Social icons are skipped; the locale switcher points to a local language page; \"Manage cookies\" is a JS dialog (#) and is not listed. The site map page stands in for microsoft.com/en-us/sitemap1.aspx and is scoped to Xbox sections.",
